Given $P_s=19.8 \mathrm{~mm}\begin{aligned}
&amp; n_A=0.1 \\
&amp; n_B=\frac{178.2}{18}=9.9
\end{aligned}$
According to Raoult's law
$\begin{gathered}
\frac{P_s-P}{P_s}=\frac{n_A}{n_A+n_B} \\
\frac{19.8-P}{19.8}=\frac{0.1}{9.9+0.1}
\end{gathered}$
or
$\begin{aligned}
198-10 P &amp; =19.8 \times 0.1 \\
10 P &amp; =198-1.98 \\
10 P &amp; =196.02 \\
P &amp; =19.602 \mathrm{~mm}
\end{aligned}$
